===== AGENTS.md =====
executable: false

# AGENTS.md

Guidance for Codex and other coding agents working in this TypeScript library.

## Project Conventions

- Use pnpm for all package management and scripts.
- Keep implementation code in `source/` and Vitest coverage in `test/`.
- Treat this package as Node 24+ and ESM-only. Do not add CommonJS compatibility unless explicitly requested.
- Do not add Prettier. Linting is handled by Oxlint, and formatting is handled by Oxfmt.
- Use Zod for external input validation and anywhere runtime validation is needed.

## Code Changes

- Keep the public API intentional. Export from `source/index.ts` deliberately, and do not expose internal modules by accident.
- Keep CLI entry points thin. Parse arguments and handle process I/O in CLI files, but put reusable behavior in normal library modules.
- When public API or CLI behavior changes, update `README.md` and tests.
- Prefer small, direct dependencies when they materially simplify the implementation.
- Update or add Vitest tests for every behavior change.
- Update the fallow boundary rules and Semgrep checks when architecture or security expectations change.

## Verification

- Before handoff, run `pnpm run release:check`.
- Use smaller targeted checks while iterating, such as `pnpm run test`, `pnpm run lint`, `pnpm run deps:lint`, or `pnpm run security:lint`.
- `pnpm run security:lint` uses Semgrep; install Semgrep or uv if neither is available.

===== .fallowrc.jsonc =====
executable: false

{
  // Architecture gate for `deps:lint`. These five rules keep `source/` layered
  // correctly: no import cycles, no unresolved or undeclared imports, no
  // reaching into `test/`, and no devDependencies in shipped code. Fallow's
  // dead-code, duplication, and complexity analyses are deliberately off so
  // this stays a focused architecture check rather than a code-quality gate.
  // Declared explicitly: the package entry points resolve into `dist/`, which is
  // ignored below, so without this the source tree is unreachable and the
  // boundary rules silently pass instead of failing.
  "entry": ["source/index.ts", "source/cli.ts"],
  "ignorePatterns": ["dist/**", "coverage/**"],
  "rules": {
    "circular-dependencies": "error",
    "unresolved-imports": "error",
    "unlisted-dependencies": "error",
    "dev-dependencies-in-production": "error",
    "boundary-violation": "error",

    // Not part of the architecture gate.
    "unused-files": "off",
    "unused-exports": "off",
    "unused-types": "off",
    "unused-dependencies": "off",
    // Kept on: every scaffolded devDependency is executed by a script or wired
    // into tsconfig/vitest, so an unused entry means something was added and
    // never hooked up. Set to "warn" if that is too strict for your project.
    "unused-dev-dependencies": "error",
    "unused-optional-dependencies": "off",
    "unused-enum-members": "off",
    "unused-class-members": "off",
    "duplicate-exports": "off",
    "re-export-cycle": "off",
    "type-only-dependencies": "off",
    "test-only-dependencies": "off",
    "stale-suppressions": "off"
  },
  "boundaries": {
    "zones": [
      { "name": "source", "patterns": ["source/**"] },
      { "name": "test", "patterns": ["test/**"] }
    ],
    "rules": [
      { "from": "source", "allow": [] },
      { "from": "test", "allow": ["source"] }
    ]
  }
}

